    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode collision de-duplication in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\nThe step already computes the base code `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D`). I added collision handling:\n\n- Injected `OwnerRepository` into `service(...)` (resolved by type, so the `owners.POST.yml` `assignCode` step needs no change).\n- Collect the `customerCode`s of all existing owners via `findAll()` \u2014 the same pre-save iteration pattern used by the sibling `AssignHouseholdId`/`EnsureIdentityUnique` steps. Since `assignCode` runs before `SaveOwner`, `findAll()` returns only owners that predate this create.\n- If the base code collides, append `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and incrementing to the smallest value that yields a unique code (`NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`, then `-3`, \u2026). The de-duplicated value is set as the owner's `customerCode`.\n\n**Why no YAML/entity changes were needed:** the pipeline wires `assignCode` before `save` under `transaction` governance already, and OfficeFloor injects the `OwnerRepository` bean by type.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The existing `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` (the only test class) passes. Its docstring notes a genuine hash collision can't be forced black-box because telephone-uniqueness already blocks identical `normalizedTelephone + lastName` inputs, so it asserts the rule's guarantee (distinct owners get distinct codes), which the new logic preserves while now also handling the collision case explicitly.",
